Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||12-28-2000||07:04 PM||||how do you take off the map pockets without damaging them?  i have the panel off and the screws seem to be in from the inside of the pockets.  problem is the vinyl is covering them.  what do i do?||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-28-2000||07:29 PM||||Look closely at the back side of the panel and you will see the nuts that hold it in place.  The pockets themselves have studs built into them.  There are "speed nuts" on the backside......I remove the jute backing around each nut  (it's pre-cut) and use a pair of pliers to unscrew the nuts.<P>I hope this helps.....it's a little hard to describe. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||12-28-2000||07:36 PM||||hey i thought that might be it but didnt want to risk it.  i know just what you mean.  thanx a ton.  time to get to work.  if all turns out right ill post some pics of them when im done.  im gettin rid of the carpet and goin with some vinyl.  if i really like it i may go for leather later or something.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE  88FORMULA<BR>KissMySSFiero@netzero.net<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">  <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-28-2000||07:39 PM||||No problem.   Take it easy removing the old carpet.......it's on there pretty good!||||reg||1
